WEBVTT

00:12.600 --> 00:13.720
[gunshot]

00:23.200 --> 00:26.680
♪ Take a little walk
To the edge of town ♪

00:26.760 --> 00:29.120
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

00:30.880 --> 00:33.120
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

00:33.200 --> 00:35.160
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

00:35.240 --> 00:38.560
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

00:39.120 --> 00:43.360
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

00:43.440 --> 00:45.360
♪ In the humming wires ♪

00:45.440 --> 00:46.720
♪ Hey man, you know ♪

00:46.800 --> 00:48.640
♪ You're never coming back ♪

00:48.760 --> 00:50.680
♪ Past the square
Past the bridge ♪

00:50.760 --> 00:53.440
♪ Past the mills
Past the stacks ♪

00:55.800 --> 00:58.160
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

00:58.240 --> 01:00.000
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

01:00.080 --> 01:02.320
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

01:02.400 --> 01:04.560
♪ A red right hand ♪

01:09.640 --> 01:11.480
[Arthur] Watch out, John-Boy,
he has got a strong left.

01:11.560 --> 01:14.640
-[Tommy] Arthur, John, Finn. Come here.
-[indistinct chatter]

01:15.760 --> 01:17.240
[horse neighs]

01:21.600 --> 01:23.320
[Arthur] All right, what is it?

01:28.880 --> 01:32.280
This letter says that Dad's dead.

01:39.680 --> 01:42.960
He was in Boston
in a bar called the Mickey Free.

01:43.680 --> 01:46.080
Two men waiting in an alley.
He was shot twice.

01:49.080 --> 01:50.760
Who's Rosie Rice?

01:52.400 --> 01:53.720
Some fucking whore.

01:53.800 --> 01:56.800
She is a woman
who took the trouble to write to us.

01:57.240 --> 01:59.920
And she wanted us to know
that during the night,

02:00.760 --> 02:03.720
while he was dying,
he asked for our forgiveness.

02:06.440 --> 02:10.360
The only thing he ever taught us
was how to kill and cut a stag.

02:10.800 --> 02:15.000
-Finn, John, you won't remember.
-I remember. Cannock Chase.

02:16.360 --> 02:18.760
Parked up at a pub called the Griffin.

02:19.200 --> 02:22.160
He got drunk and sang "Silver Dagger"
about 100 times.

02:22.240 --> 02:23.680
Yeah. One weekend.

02:24.960 --> 02:26.960
One weekend he was like that.

02:28.880 --> 02:31.000
[Tommy] The stag is to remember him.

02:31.800 --> 02:34.440
We eat and then we forget him.

02:35.800 --> 02:37.920
No need to forgive him. Agreed?

02:42.680 --> 02:45.040
John, I have to say this.

02:45.120 --> 02:47.600
You can name your new baby after him
if you like.

02:47.680 --> 02:48.800
No.

02:49.720 --> 02:51.520
Arthur, and I won't even ask.

02:54.720 --> 02:56.200
So his name dies.

02:56.920 --> 02:59.840
It's been in the family for a long time,
but now it's gone.

03:01.720 --> 03:04.240
All right, that's done. Fuck him.

03:06.160 --> 03:09.080
Before we cook and eat,
there's some business.

03:09.160 --> 03:10.160
Boys!

03:21.560 --> 03:25.760
I wanted to say this out here, 'cause
I don't trust the maids in the house.

03:28.000 --> 03:29.600
There's gonna be a robbery.

03:39.560 --> 03:42.520
-I wish to confess.
-There's no confessional today.

03:42.600 --> 03:44.040
The name's Shelby.

03:51.720 --> 03:54.120
-[creaking]
-[door closes]

03:58.360 --> 04:00.440
Bless me, Father, for I have sinned.

04:00.760 --> 04:02.440
Today is a holy day.

04:02.520 --> 04:05.960
Look, I came. I made myself.

04:07.000 --> 04:08.160
You been drinking?

04:09.240 --> 04:10.480
I couldn't sleep.

04:12.960 --> 04:15.840
I tried to get enough down me
to get myself to sleep, but...

04:17.839 --> 04:21.040
I just do these night vigils
by myself, thinking...

04:21.720 --> 04:23.720
How long since your last confession?

04:26.680 --> 04:28.040
I don't remember.

04:29.040 --> 04:32.400
Mrs. Shelby,
do you have something to confess?

04:32.480 --> 04:37.120
Do you know it is actually "Gray"?
My name is, um, Elizabeth Gray.

04:38.280 --> 04:41.120
Yeah. Do you think God calls me
Pol or Polly?

04:44.040 --> 04:45.840
Voice calls me Pol.

04:47.960 --> 04:49.600
You hear a voice?

04:51.480 --> 04:55.760
-Yeah. Like Bernadette heard a voice.
-And what does the voice say?

04:57.960 --> 04:59.240
"Murderer."

05:03.320 --> 05:05.120
It says this to you?

05:06.840 --> 05:09.400
It's in my head.
Who else would it be talking to?

05:10.800 --> 05:14.080
And are you a murderer?

05:15.040 --> 05:17.600
If you're talking about the law, then...

05:17.680 --> 05:19.920
[footsteps approach]

05:20.080 --> 05:21.680
-Yes.
-[knocking on door]

05:21.760 --> 05:24.680
-I'll be out in a moment, Peter.
-[Peter] Yes, Father.

05:25.160 --> 05:26.800
[footsteps fading]

05:29.280 --> 05:33.400
Are you saying
you want to confess to a murder?

05:34.800 --> 05:35.840
[Polly] No.

05:37.360 --> 05:40.160
My confession is that I feel no regret.

05:41.240 --> 05:46.360
He was a policeman,
he was a bad man, he hurt me.

05:49.840 --> 05:53.320
I do the things I do
so that my son doesn't have to do them.

05:55.360 --> 05:58.280
It's just the wiping away of the shit
from under your feet.

05:58.360 --> 06:01.320
The taking of any human life
is a mortal sin.

06:01.400 --> 06:06.080
No, the unjust taking of a human life
is a mortal sin.

06:06.480 --> 06:08.200
Look it up. Look who did it.

06:08.280 --> 06:11.040
Moses, Samson, Lord Kitchener.

06:11.600 --> 06:15.240
Are you saying
you took the life of a policeman?

06:15.640 --> 06:16.880
[Polly sighs]

06:20.560 --> 06:21.760
[creaking]

06:23.400 --> 06:24.600
Oh, Father.

06:27.600 --> 06:29.840
[sobbing]
Now there is another life to be taken.

06:30.120 --> 06:35.920
If there is a voice telling you
to take a life, you must ignore it.

06:36.000 --> 06:39.240
The voice doesn't tell me.
The voice asks me.

06:39.320 --> 06:41.280
It says, "Pol,

06:41.880 --> 06:44.600
does this way of excusing
a murder still work

06:45.160 --> 06:50.680
if the life that is going to be taken
is a consecrated man?"

06:52.400 --> 06:54.040
He's a man of the cloth.

06:55.000 --> 06:56.600
He's a holy man.

06:57.840 --> 06:59.240
What kind of holy man?

07:00.280 --> 07:01.520
[sighing]

07:07.080 --> 07:08.360
[door opens]

07:11.120 --> 07:13.040
[footsteps fading]

07:17.920 --> 07:19.120
[door closes]

07:20.960 --> 07:22.240
-[Esme] It's not fair.
-[door opens]

07:22.520 --> 07:25.720
They're off drinking and shooting rifles
as we sit here.

07:25.800 --> 07:27.880
-[door closes]
-Listen to the mugs swearing,

07:27.960 --> 07:31.720
spitting on the bloody floor
for us to fucking wipe up!

07:33.040 --> 07:36.320
Without men here,
they'd be like dogs pissing up the wall.

07:36.920 --> 07:39.080
I was just saying it's not fair.

07:40.080 --> 07:42.040
The men are down there like lords.

07:43.080 --> 07:44.680
Esme, just...

07:46.040 --> 07:47.560
Get on with it.

07:48.120 --> 07:50.280
I'm bloody five months gone.

07:50.920 --> 07:52.640
[sniffing]

07:54.480 --> 07:58.480
-[sighs] Forgot the combination.
-24-8-22.

07:59.840 --> 08:01.960
How do you know
the paper cash combination?

08:02.040 --> 08:04.680
-Tommy talks in his sleep.
-Shut up, Esme.

08:05.600 --> 08:06.760
[clanks]

08:07.040 --> 08:08.320
[groans]

08:10.080 --> 08:11.560
He's changed the combination.

08:14.240 --> 08:17.360
-[Lizzie] You've put it in wrong.
-No, I haven't.

08:20.280 --> 08:21.640
Your hands are shaking.

08:22.360 --> 08:23.360
[creaks]

08:24.760 --> 08:25.880
[sniffing]

08:37.720 --> 08:40.840
And actually, I am sleeping with Tommy,
okay? Now and then.

08:41.200 --> 08:43.640
Because he wants to, now and then.
When the mood takes him.

08:44.240 --> 08:47.840
Except we don't sleep. It's hard to sleep
bent over a desk, isn't it?

08:49.360 --> 08:50.400
Happy?

08:52.640 --> 08:54.640
-[door opens]
-[women talking indistinctly]

08:54.720 --> 08:56.880
None of it's fucking fair.

09:01.040 --> 09:02.560
[Tommy] It's two hours' work.

09:02.640 --> 09:04.520
Bit of grease on your cuffs,
and that's it.

09:04.600 --> 09:06.280
Tommy, should I really be here for this?

09:06.360 --> 09:08.040
I've cleared it with Polly, Michael.

09:08.120 --> 09:10.600
There's no way around it.
We need you to know.

09:10.680 --> 09:14.360
Who the fuck wants to buy
27 stolen armored cars?

09:14.440 --> 09:15.640
A foolish man.

09:15.720 --> 09:17.720
[Michael] And how much
is this foolish man paying?

09:17.800 --> 09:21.920
£150,000. Cash, diamonds and sapphires.

09:23.040 --> 09:24.920
So that's 20 for you, Charlie.

09:26.440 --> 09:28.480
Isiah, there's 5 to you.

09:28.560 --> 09:31.800
The rest we take to America
to invest in legally-acquired property.

09:32.120 --> 09:34.920
Assets bought
with untraceable income resold,

09:35.000 --> 09:37.440
and the profits reinvested
to make sure it's clean.

09:37.520 --> 09:39.080
[Arthur] And after that, I suppose,

09:39.160 --> 09:44.000
the whole business will be like that stag
hanging up over there, right, Tom?

09:44.080 --> 09:45.880
Well, with profits on this scale,

09:45.960 --> 09:48.800
we'll be in a position
to stop the off-track business for good.

09:48.880 --> 09:51.400
Keep the pubs, stop the protection.

09:51.880 --> 09:54.720
Horses for the sport
and race days for a lark.

09:56.320 --> 09:59.440
I made a promise to Charles' mother.

09:59.520 --> 10:02.800
Now, I also made a promise to Linda.

10:04.240 --> 10:05.320
I know.

10:06.160 --> 10:08.000
I can see it in your eyes, man.

10:08.080 --> 10:09.880
Part of the reason for doing this last job

10:09.960 --> 10:13.840
is so you'll be set up
when you do decide to walk away.

10:15.160 --> 10:16.680
[Strong] Look at you, Arthur.

10:17.640 --> 10:20.000
A man that wanted to live a clean life,

10:20.080 --> 10:23.560
but here you are signing up for
the biggest robbery of all.

10:24.600 --> 10:26.080
I have to hand it to you, Tom.

10:26.520 --> 10:29.040
-You're a smart man.
-You in or out, Charlie?

10:34.840 --> 10:35.920
Curly?

10:36.960 --> 10:38.240
Shouldn't have killed the stag, Tommy.

10:38.320 --> 10:39.880
-Oh, shut up. Shut up.
-Bad luck.

10:41.160 --> 10:44.520
How do we know this foolish man will
hand over the diamonds when we're done?

10:44.600 --> 10:46.160
We don't.

10:46.240 --> 10:47.600
But that's another business.

10:49.480 --> 10:52.640
Right, let's cook some meat.

10:57.440 --> 10:59.040
[banging on door]

10:59.120 --> 11:02.080
[Esme] Can't wait to part
with their money, stupid bastards.

11:02.160 --> 11:04.000
[Linda] It's all right, it's me.

11:07.600 --> 11:08.640
[door closes]

11:08.720 --> 11:12.280
Arthur said you'd be short-staffed today
because they are on a works outing.

11:12.360 --> 11:13.720
[Esme] Piss-up, actually.

11:14.760 --> 11:17.880
I brought sandwiches
and this lemonade I made myself.

11:17.960 --> 11:19.080
[typewriter keys clacking]

11:19.160 --> 11:22.400
I'll make tea and empty ashtrays,
but I won't handle money or slips.

11:23.960 --> 11:26.880
Arthur says what you do here
is illegal, but not immoral.

11:27.760 --> 11:30.000
[Esme] Depends what time
you get here, Linda.

11:30.840 --> 11:32.360
And anyway,

11:32.440 --> 11:35.720
I thought I'd offer you my physical and
spiritual support in your time of need.

11:35.800 --> 11:37.200
Oh, Linda, if you want to be a help,

11:37.280 --> 11:40.440
run up to the shops
and get me 20 Senior Service.

11:40.960 --> 11:43.760
-Lizzie'll give you the change.
-[chuckles] No, I won't.

11:43.840 --> 11:46.480
Actually, I'll use my own money, Polly.

11:47.320 --> 11:50.760
And before you ladies decide to find me
so amusing, I have a message for you.

11:50.840 --> 11:51.880
Oh, God, no, Linda.

11:51.960 --> 11:53.680
I've been to church already. Have you?

11:53.760 --> 11:55.920
It's not a message from God, Polly.

11:56.000 --> 11:59.040
-It's from Jessie Eden.
-Who's Jessie Eden?

11:59.120 --> 12:01.960
[Linda] She's the lady shop steward
at the Lucas factory in Sparkhill.

12:02.040 --> 12:03.360
[Esme] Lady shop steward?

12:03.440 --> 12:06.880
She's bringing all the female workers
in the spot-welding and wire-cutting shops

12:06.960 --> 12:08.080
out on strike for the day.

12:08.360 --> 12:11.040
In protest at being made to work
on a holy day.

12:11.360 --> 12:14.560
Poor conditions, lack of holidays,
unsanitary lavatory provisions

12:14.640 --> 12:16.640
and lower pay for female workers.

12:17.200 --> 12:20.200
Apparently, all the female
factory workers in the city

12:20.280 --> 12:22.240
are joining the protest in sympathy

12:22.480 --> 12:24.280
and will walk out of their places of work
at 9:00 a.m.

12:24.360 --> 12:26.520
-to march on the Bull Ring.
-[banging on door]

12:27.440 --> 12:30.160
All oppressed female workers welcome.

12:30.240 --> 12:32.000
Them bastards down there shooting deer.

12:32.080 --> 12:34.320
Me five months gone,
sat here like a pudding.

12:34.400 --> 12:36.680
[Linda] Only one outside lavatory
between the lot of us.

12:36.760 --> 12:37.920
Not consulted.

12:38.000 --> 12:39.720
-Bent over a fucking desk.
-[banging continues]

12:40.040 --> 12:44.200
Ladies, I honestly believe those who march
on Good Friday have God on their side.

12:44.520 --> 12:45.920
-[banging on door]
-[man] It's 9 o'clock, ladies!

12:46.000 --> 12:47.200
Open the fucking door!

12:49.920 --> 12:51.120
Fuck it.

12:52.000 --> 12:54.040
I'm not in the mood today.

12:57.400 --> 12:59.160
Let's go to the Bull Ring.

12:59.880 --> 13:01.200
Hallelujah!

13:01.280 --> 13:03.400
[rock music playing]

13:34.040 --> 13:35.600
[whistle blows]

13:38.520 --> 13:40.120
[Michael] The foolish man?

13:41.480 --> 13:42.800
Not quite.

14:02.040 --> 14:03.600
I'm sorry I came unannounced.

14:04.240 --> 14:05.280
What do you want?

14:05.880 --> 14:07.400
We need proof.

14:08.280 --> 14:10.360
Proof of what? [clears throat]

14:10.440 --> 14:12.440
You said the priest is a traitor.

14:12.760 --> 14:14.360
We need to know how you know.

14:15.400 --> 14:16.760
The proof is my word.

14:18.680 --> 14:21.080
If he is involved, I'm out.
He needs to die.

14:21.680 --> 14:23.320
Are you always so violent?

14:26.280 --> 14:27.800
I killed a stag today,

14:28.760 --> 14:30.360
and it hurt me to do it.

14:31.640 --> 14:36.200
But I treated it with respect,
and the spare meat will go to poor people.

14:38.000 --> 14:41.920
It will grieve me far less
to put a bullet in the priest's face.

14:44.840 --> 14:47.080
Will you not sit when a duchess sits?

14:48.600 --> 14:51.120
I'm told you're part of the deal.
Is that true?

14:52.280 --> 14:55.440
The Royal Court in Tbilisi
actually worked very efficiently.

14:55.520 --> 14:58.200
Ah, I see. And it worked like this, eh?

14:58.280 --> 15:02.040
[Tatiana] There were lots of corridors
and small rooms.

15:02.120 --> 15:03.360
Attics.

15:03.440 --> 15:05.800
There were no rules there.
Deals were done.

15:05.880 --> 15:09.680
Brothers gave sisters, aunts gave uncles,
fathers gave daughters and servants.

15:09.760 --> 15:10.920
[glass clinks]

15:12.560 --> 15:14.920
It was my aunt's idea that I came alone.

15:17.640 --> 15:19.440
She is in charge of this.

15:27.600 --> 15:30.400
When there are no rules,
women take charge.

15:31.080 --> 15:34.560
They understand that the power they have
comes through silent agreements.

15:34.640 --> 15:38.440
I've promised I will do everything I can
to make this plan work.

15:38.520 --> 15:41.400
My aunt assumed you would want me
as part of the deal.

15:43.320 --> 15:44.640
I will tell her she's wrong.

15:44.720 --> 15:46.880
-[footsteps approach]
-[door opens]

15:47.480 --> 15:50.240
[chuckling]
Tommy, you ain't gonna believe this, man.

15:50.760 --> 15:53.040
I just phoned the garrison, right?
I just spoke to Billy.

15:53.120 --> 15:57.720
He says Polly, Esme and Lizzie have
gone on fucking strike.

15:57.800 --> 15:59.080
[laughs]

15:59.160 --> 16:01.400
-They what?
-They've gone on fucking strike!

16:02.240 --> 16:03.800
Half of Birmingham is out.

16:03.880 --> 16:06.760
The female half, they're all out,
every single one of them.

16:06.840 --> 16:08.120
Quakers put 'em up to it.

16:09.520 --> 16:10.680
Who's watching the shop?

16:11.240 --> 16:12.400
[John] Polly's locked it up.

16:13.200 --> 16:15.840
See, Good Friday's
one of our best days for takings.

16:17.280 --> 16:21.160
All the men get drunk.
The races are all fixed.

16:21.240 --> 16:24.200
It's like picking apples
off the lowest branches.

16:24.280 --> 16:25.560
Hey, John?

16:26.080 --> 16:27.160
Hmm, yes.

16:27.480 --> 16:29.200
Then your business is very easy.

16:31.440 --> 16:33.280
-Was Linda with them?
-You know,

16:33.880 --> 16:36.800
Billy said that Polly jumped
in the fucking Bull Ring,

16:36.880 --> 16:39.840
just pissed out of her mind,
started going on about revolution,

16:39.920 --> 16:41.160
screaming to the rooftops.

16:41.680 --> 16:43.400
Was Linda with them?

16:44.520 --> 16:45.640
Yeah.

16:46.480 --> 16:48.360
Then it was Linda's idea.

16:48.840 --> 16:51.560
-Linda's a smart woman.
-[footsteps approach]

16:57.880 --> 16:59.040
John.

17:00.200 --> 17:01.920
There's a Bentley in the drive outside.

17:02.000 --> 17:04.119
I want you to go out
and put a nail in its tire.

17:04.200 --> 17:07.000
It's Good Friday,
so there'll be no garages open.

17:07.079 --> 17:08.680
The lady will have to spend the night.

17:09.119 --> 17:11.440
Then I want you and the boys
to all go home.

17:11.520 --> 17:14.119
You take Charlie, put him with
Arthur and Linda for the night.

17:14.200 --> 17:16.160
They can use the practice.

17:19.359 --> 17:21.280
-You want to put a nail...
-Yeah.

17:21.599 --> 17:23.240
-You heard me.
-Yeah.

17:23.640 --> 17:26.280
Right. Nice to meet you.

17:30.520 --> 17:32.920
Why do you need to put a nail in the tire?

17:33.640 --> 17:36.200
I want it so neither of us
can change our minds.

17:43.120 --> 17:44.440
[creaking]

17:46.400 --> 17:48.200
[clanking]

18:00.160 --> 18:01.760
[John] We came back early.

18:07.280 --> 18:09.160
Polly didn't finish the count yesterday.

18:10.000 --> 18:11.120
Hmm.

18:12.040 --> 18:13.640
So you thought you could take a tenner.

18:14.400 --> 18:16.000
I thought I'd finish the count.

18:20.480 --> 18:22.320
[both grunting]

18:23.760 --> 18:24.880
[John] Hey!

18:24.960 --> 18:27.560
Esme, I've told you.
Stay off the snow until the baby's born.

18:27.640 --> 18:30.600
[Esme] It does no harm, passes the time.

18:30.680 --> 18:33.520
-Knocks down the walls.
-Listen. [grunts]

18:34.680 --> 18:36.320
[panting] Listen.

18:37.520 --> 18:39.520
I know you miss the traveling.

18:40.240 --> 18:41.920
It's all gonna be all right.

18:42.880 --> 18:44.840
It's like being a hen in a coop.

18:48.920 --> 18:51.120
Remember that house in Lichfield?

18:52.240 --> 18:54.760
The one the bailiff
used to throw you out of?

18:54.840 --> 18:56.400
Throw you in a ditch.

18:58.000 --> 19:00.440
I'm gonna buy that fucking house.

19:01.120 --> 19:03.160
Big as Tommy's and more land.

19:04.480 --> 19:06.320
If you feel cooped up,

19:07.000 --> 19:11.080
we'll take a wagon, camp out by the ditch.

19:12.520 --> 19:13.720
How?

19:16.080 --> 19:17.440
[sniffles]

19:18.160 --> 19:20.280
It's all gonna change, Esme.

19:26.200 --> 19:27.880
[Tatiana] This is not your bedroom.

19:28.480 --> 19:30.920
This is not where
you slept with your wife.

19:31.680 --> 19:33.240
Do you ride horses?

19:33.720 --> 19:34.840
No.

19:34.920 --> 19:38.880
I would need to open my legs in
a public place, and that is not allowed.

19:39.560 --> 19:40.720
You drink whiskey?

19:41.240 --> 19:42.320
No.

19:42.840 --> 19:45.920
It tastes like men. I prefer wine.

19:47.760 --> 19:48.840
Cars?

19:49.440 --> 19:50.560
No.

19:51.200 --> 19:53.800
So, diamonds are your only love, eh?

19:53.880 --> 19:55.720
-Sapphires?
-[chuckles]

19:57.240 --> 19:59.040
They're just a currency.

19:59.800 --> 20:03.280
Well, you know,
if it was me who had all them jewels,

20:05.840 --> 20:08.560
I think I'd just sit with them,

20:09.440 --> 20:10.680
look at them,

20:12.000 --> 20:13.040
touch them.

20:13.120 --> 20:14.720
Izabella does that sometimes.

20:15.160 --> 20:16.320
Late at night.

20:18.360 --> 20:21.760
I swear she puts one of the biggest
sapphires into her body for pleasure,

20:21.840 --> 20:24.640
and walks up the stairs
to breakfast with it still in place.

20:24.720 --> 20:25.960
[laughs]

20:27.480 --> 20:29.720
-And it stays in there all day?
-Yeah.

20:29.800 --> 20:30.800
Oh.

20:31.960 --> 20:33.520
What is your weakness?

20:35.840 --> 20:38.440
Talking about duchesses
with sapphires inside of them.

20:38.520 --> 20:39.600
Mmm.

20:40.640 --> 20:42.760
I think I already know your weakness.

20:47.680 --> 20:49.600
I can get a fuck whenever I want, love.

20:50.000 --> 20:51.080
Yes.

20:52.360 --> 20:54.080
But I am a duchess.

20:55.600 --> 20:57.600
And I am under you like a horse.

20:57.680 --> 20:59.640
-I'm like a telegram.
-[chuckling]

21:01.640 --> 21:04.080
"A telegram"?
I don't think your English is so good.

21:05.240 --> 21:08.680
Or maybe you should listen more carefully
to what I have to say.

21:09.760 --> 21:10.880
Hmm?

21:11.960 --> 21:14.200
I have a message for you, Mr. Shelby.

21:16.160 --> 21:20.960
As a duchess, I can show you
what is possible for a man like you.

21:22.360 --> 21:25.320
A man in a house like this.

21:26.320 --> 21:30.080
Right now, you hide inside it like a boy
who's broken in through the window.

21:31.400 --> 21:34.280
Why did we come to a bedroom for this?
Hmm?

21:35.760 --> 21:36.960
In your own house?

21:42.480 --> 21:43.520
[door opens]

21:45.600 --> 21:48.280
-[Tatiana laughs]
-It's a loaded fucking weapon.

21:48.360 --> 21:52.080
We could fuck by the fire with the maids
standing to attention and watching, huh?

21:52.160 --> 21:53.200
What can they do?

21:53.280 --> 21:54.400
-Give it here.
-Nothing.

21:54.480 --> 21:56.920
There are no rules for you. Hmm?

21:57.000 --> 21:58.080
Give me the fucking gun.

21:58.160 --> 22:00.680
You have maids here.
You can bring a maid into the room.

22:00.760 --> 22:02.720
What can I do about that? Nothing.

22:02.800 --> 22:05.800
-Give me the fucking gun, now.
-You have power.

22:06.040 --> 22:08.800
Everyone does what you tell them to do.

22:08.880 --> 22:13.000
Your brothers, your soldiers,
no one can stop you.

22:13.080 --> 22:14.200
Don't point the fucking weapon at me.

22:14.280 --> 22:15.800
I can be an actress.

22:16.560 --> 22:18.160
Who do you want me to be?

22:19.160 --> 22:20.240
Your dead wife?

22:20.320 --> 22:21.880
Now, that's enough.
Give me the fucking gun!

22:21.960 --> 22:25.120
If you don't like something,
you say stop, and it stops. Hmm?

22:25.880 --> 22:27.640
But you are afraid of it.

22:27.720 --> 22:30.320
You break the law,
but you obey the rules. Why?

22:31.600 --> 22:34.360
Did you know that madness sets you free?

22:34.440 --> 22:36.840
Otherwise, we're just peasants
obeying the law.

22:39.240 --> 22:41.400
There is madness inside your head, too.
I can see that.

22:43.600 --> 22:45.600
Let a duchess show you something.

22:46.320 --> 22:47.760
[footsteps thudding]

22:48.760 --> 22:49.840
[door opens]

22:53.640 --> 22:55.040
[clicking]

22:57.240 --> 22:58.600
[gun barrel turns]

22:59.840 --> 23:02.280
I emptied the chamber,
except for one bullet.

23:02.360 --> 23:04.720
-No! No, please.
-This is a game we used to play.

23:05.440 --> 23:06.480
No.

23:07.200 --> 23:09.080
-Watch.
-Do not fucking do this.

23:09.160 --> 23:11.240
No. Look at me.

23:11.920 --> 23:12.960
Don't do this.

23:13.040 --> 23:14.080
-[clicks]
-No!

23:14.160 --> 23:16.040
Give me the fucking thing.

23:18.120 --> 23:20.440
It brings you alive. You won't try it?

23:20.520 --> 23:22.080
No, I do not want to try!

23:22.160 --> 23:27.120
And I do not want your mad fucking
Russian brains all over me fucking walls.

23:27.200 --> 23:28.960
I survive each time by the will of God.

23:29.040 --> 23:30.400
Get to fucking bed, now!

23:30.480 --> 23:32.280
[Tatiana] I already called a maid.

23:32.360 --> 23:33.520
[Tommy] Fucking...

23:35.160 --> 23:37.160
[footsteps thudding]

23:46.560 --> 23:47.680
You see?

23:48.640 --> 23:50.280
You are afraid.

23:52.480 --> 23:55.080
Like a boy who's broken in
through the window.

23:56.280 --> 23:58.920
I need to educate you
in how to run a house like this.

23:59.000 --> 24:00.240
[footsteps approach]

24:00.760 --> 24:02.200
Yes. Come down.

24:02.720 --> 24:03.760
Pour us a drink.

24:03.880 --> 24:05.960
Mary, go back to bed, please.

24:06.200 --> 24:08.920
You go back to bed, please.
This woman is drunk.

24:09.200 --> 24:10.960
That's all right, sir.
Should I pour whiskey?

24:11.040 --> 24:12.760
-Yes, he will have whiskey.
-No, go back to bed.

24:13.600 --> 24:15.680
He will have whiskey and I will have wine!

24:16.440 --> 24:17.760
-Mary, go back to bed.
-[Tatiana] There.

24:17.840 --> 24:19.440
-In an old house like this...
-[Tommy] Stop fucking talking.

24:19.520 --> 24:21.920
-...the servants expect it.
-Mary, go back to bed! Do as I say!

24:22.000 --> 24:23.640
Normally, if there's a call
after midnight,

24:23.720 --> 24:25.760
the maid who comes in
is the one in love with the master,

24:25.840 --> 24:28.760
-but she is not in love with you.
-This is not fucking Russia!

24:29.760 --> 24:32.600
[softly] Please, Mary.
Go back to bed, hey?

24:46.720 --> 24:48.760
I know your weakness, Tommy.

24:51.520 --> 24:52.960
It's freedom.

24:54.880 --> 24:56.120
Madness.

24:57.400 --> 24:58.720
Killing.

25:03.520 --> 25:08.360
I am the first one who understands you.

25:17.800 --> 25:19.360
[footsteps thudding]

25:55.120 --> 25:56.880
I found her perfume.

25:58.360 --> 25:59.680
Put it on.

26:04.240 --> 26:07.400
What proof do you have
that the priest is a spy?

26:07.760 --> 26:10.160
I told you. I give you my word.

26:28.520 --> 26:29.960
Then kill him.

26:33.000 --> 26:36.480
From now on, you must do
everything that you want to do.

27:05.600 --> 27:07.880
There'll be two of us for breakfast
this morning, Mary.

27:07.960 --> 27:10.400
She's gone for a walk by the river.

27:10.480 --> 27:13.040
-[Mary] The lady left, sir.
-[cutlery clinks]

27:13.200 --> 27:14.920
Left? How?

27:15.560 --> 27:16.720
She took your car.

27:17.960 --> 27:19.000
She what?

27:19.080 --> 27:22.560
She was in a terrible hurry.
She said she had your permission.

27:23.080 --> 27:26.760
She told David to go to the garage
to get a new tire for the Bentley.

27:26.840 --> 27:28.480
She said you could use that.

27:29.360 --> 27:31.520
And why the hell would you listen to her?

27:31.920 --> 27:33.480
The way she said it, sir.

28:07.000 --> 28:08.480
[door closes]

28:08.560 --> 28:11.280
-[Arthur] How was she, Tom?
-Talkative, yeah.

28:11.360 --> 28:12.400
Hmm.

28:12.840 --> 28:14.520
I was fucking working, all right?

28:14.880 --> 28:15.920
Yeah.

28:17.800 --> 28:20.000
From what she said,
when she was out of her fucking mind,

28:20.080 --> 28:22.440
I'm pretty certain
the treasury is underneath the house.

28:22.520 --> 28:23.520
What have you got?

28:23.600 --> 28:27.000
Our Ada got this from the British Library
using her scholar's pass.

28:29.440 --> 28:30.720
[Tommy] She talks about her aunt

28:30.800 --> 28:32.720
coming up the stairs
to have breakfast in the morning,

28:32.800 --> 28:35.760
which means
it has to be in the building somewhere.

28:35.840 --> 28:38.080
[Arthur] Wine cellar. Septic.

28:38.560 --> 28:40.240
Kitchen cellar.

28:40.320 --> 28:41.520
[John] And a tunnel under the river.

28:41.600 --> 28:43.040
They don't trust a soul in this country,

28:43.120 --> 28:46.760
so my guess is they've turned
one of the cellars into a strong room.

28:46.840 --> 28:47.920
Did you find someone, Arthur?

28:48.320 --> 28:49.720
Moss got me this.

28:49.800 --> 28:51.920
Stefan Radischevsky.

28:52.000 --> 28:54.360
He's a kid from Greet,
lives in Cheltenham.

28:54.440 --> 28:58.160
Dad's a Russian. He has dreams of
owning a pub, but he's got a record.

28:58.440 --> 29:00.080
-Breaking and entering.
-[Arthur] Hmm.

29:00.160 --> 29:01.800
-And he speaks Russian?
-Yeah.

29:01.880 --> 29:04.840
Their butler drinks in a pub
called the Masons Arms.

29:04.920 --> 29:06.080
Get to him, tell him who we are,

29:06.160 --> 29:09.040
offer him some money
if he gives the kid a job in the house.

29:09.120 --> 29:10.440
-[knocking on door]
-Wait.

29:11.000 --> 29:12.680
Talk to the kid,

29:12.760 --> 29:15.040
offer him one of the pubs
we took off the Italians

29:15.120 --> 29:18.360
if he works in the house for four weeks,
keeps his ears open.

29:18.440 --> 29:19.600
All right?

29:19.680 --> 29:20.840
Come.

29:23.160 --> 29:26.040
The executive committee of
the union of bookies and allied trades

29:26.120 --> 29:27.560
will see you now, sir.

29:37.320 --> 29:38.960
[indistinct chatter]

29:40.760 --> 29:44.120
I heard you were giving speeches
off the back of a wagon, Pol.

29:44.960 --> 29:47.680
I can't remember a fucking thing.

29:47.760 --> 29:51.080
Well, Moss tells me you were threatening
to burn down the town hall.

29:51.400 --> 29:53.880
Oh, Tommy, we were having a laugh.

29:55.200 --> 29:57.560
You know, actually,
the crowd around me was bigger

29:57.640 --> 29:59.320
than the crowd around Jessie Eden.

29:59.400 --> 30:00.600
[Tommy] Who's Jessie Eden?

30:00.680 --> 30:01.840
[Polly] She's too soft.

30:01.920 --> 30:03.840
You're not gonna
break the capitalist system

30:03.920 --> 30:06.600
talking about
separate lavatories for women.

30:06.680 --> 30:07.760
Who is Jessie Eden?

30:08.080 --> 30:09.480
She's a new best friend.

30:09.560 --> 30:11.560
Shop steward at the Lucas factory.

30:11.640 --> 30:13.520
A woman shop steward, I've heard of her.

30:13.600 --> 30:15.760
There is a leaflet here
if you want to take a look, Tommy.

30:17.920 --> 30:19.400
[Lizzie clears throat]

30:20.880 --> 30:23.880
So, separate lavatory?
Is that it? Is that what you want?

30:24.520 --> 30:25.520
I don't know what you want.

30:25.600 --> 30:27.960
You have to tell me what it is
that you want and then I'll know.

30:28.920 --> 30:32.800
Actually, we want to know
about the robbery you're planning.

30:32.880 --> 30:35.240
Not the factory robbery. The other one.

30:35.880 --> 30:38.120
The one you're not
telling the women about.

30:38.560 --> 30:40.280
-John has a big mouth.
-[Esme] No.

30:41.480 --> 30:46.120
Arthur's got a big mouth.
Arthur told Linda, Linda told me.

30:47.880 --> 30:49.480
-Polly?
-Read the leaflet, Tommy.

30:49.560 --> 30:52.440
Ladies, why don't I
talk to Tommy privately,

30:52.520 --> 30:54.760
and then I'll report
back to you faithfully.

30:54.840 --> 30:57.480
You're not just gonna take payment
from the Russians, are you, Tommy?

30:57.880 --> 30:59.880
You're going to clean them out,
is that right?

30:59.960 --> 31:01.040
[Lizzie] Esme?

31:01.680 --> 31:04.440
So, what happens after,
when they come for us?

31:04.520 --> 31:05.920
When I'm about to give birth?

31:06.000 --> 31:08.600
Get out, get back to work.

31:08.680 --> 31:09.880
Esme, come on.

31:12.480 --> 31:15.080
-Keep us posted, won't you, sister?
-I will.

31:16.280 --> 31:17.280
[door closes]

31:19.920 --> 31:21.000
Fucking hell.

31:24.800 --> 31:26.880
So Arthur tells Linda everything, eh?

31:27.320 --> 31:30.440
She's stolen his soul
and taken it to a better place.

31:30.520 --> 31:31.560
The suburbs.

31:31.960 --> 31:34.080
Where men are honest with their wives.

31:35.440 --> 31:36.440
We can trust Lizzie.

31:37.920 --> 31:39.920
Yeah, but I can't trust Esme.

31:40.520 --> 31:42.800
I can't trust the fucking Russians
to pay me what they owe me,

31:42.880 --> 31:45.640
and I can't trust my own brother
to keep his fucking mouth shut.

31:46.880 --> 31:48.600
Did you make progress last night?

31:52.080 --> 31:53.200
Yes.

31:55.040 --> 31:58.520
John said the girl looks like
Edna Purviance from the pictures.

31:59.040 --> 32:00.920
[clicks tongue] Be careful.

32:03.960 --> 32:07.360
She's an excellent source of information
regarding the location of the merchandise.

32:07.440 --> 32:08.440
-Here we go.
-You know,

32:08.520 --> 32:11.520
there is a general lack of discipline
in this fucking company.

32:13.360 --> 32:15.080
She stayed the night.

32:16.480 --> 32:17.880
I'm working, Pol.

32:18.520 --> 32:20.960
I am working for the good of the company.

32:23.240 --> 32:24.480
You're grieving.

32:25.920 --> 32:27.640
And when you grieve,
you make bad choices.

32:28.200 --> 32:30.960
I know. I did it myself.

32:31.040 --> 32:33.080
Look. No more marches.

32:33.840 --> 32:35.320
No more fucking politics.

32:35.400 --> 32:37.800
It can kill us. All right?
Joke or no joke.

32:38.400 --> 32:39.960
Did you tell Arthur about the priest?

32:40.520 --> 32:41.920
I only told you.

32:43.200 --> 32:44.560
Thanks for the burden.

32:47.000 --> 32:48.360
[bell tolling]

32:56.400 --> 32:58.880
You were correct
not to talk over the phone.

32:58.960 --> 33:00.600
What did she say?

33:02.760 --> 33:05.960
She said there was gonna be a killing.
A holy man.

33:07.720 --> 33:10.080
And she was with the Shelbys, was she?

33:10.880 --> 33:12.080
[sighs]

33:40.280 --> 33:42.960
I suppose you have something to say
about yesterday.

33:43.600 --> 33:44.840
No.

33:44.920 --> 33:46.560
It's something else, actually.

33:50.280 --> 33:54.000
I believe Arthur has told you
about some business we're planning, Linda.

33:54.480 --> 33:56.480
Oh, there's always business, Thomas.

33:56.840 --> 34:00.240
And Arthur believes when
this business is done, it'll all be over.

34:01.640 --> 34:03.880
Arthur believes you, but I don't.

34:05.680 --> 34:06.720
[sighs]

34:06.800 --> 34:11.480
Linda, the people who have hired us
to rob the factory are very bad people.

34:12.400 --> 34:14.120
They'll not pay us, as they've promised.

34:14.199 --> 34:18.320
So, on the night of the robbery, we will
take what is ours from their treasury.

34:18.400 --> 34:20.040
And a bit more on top for luck.

34:20.320 --> 34:23.960
If you're saying you're gonna stop Arthur,
I need to know.

34:24.679 --> 34:26.280
That'll be Arthur's decision.

34:27.520 --> 34:29.840
And your plan is still to reform him, eh?

34:29.920 --> 34:32.840
-To the absolute degree of redemption.
-Mmm-hmm.

34:34.480 --> 34:38.400
Well, Arthur will walk away from this
with £30,000. We made a deal.

34:38.639 --> 34:40.000
And afterwards,

34:41.080 --> 34:43.760
you and Arthur can begin your new life.

34:48.400 --> 34:50.120
Did you say 30,000?

34:51.280 --> 34:54.560
Arthur said the estimated total proceeds
would be 150,000.

34:54.639 --> 34:57.000
-Estimated. Yes.
-A third of 150 is 50.

34:57.080 --> 34:58.440
-Why a third?
-The three brothers.

34:58.520 --> 35:00.080
-Finn is not yet a man.
-There are expenses.

35:00.160 --> 35:01.480
Of 25,000, you said.

35:01.560 --> 35:04.880
As of last night, the expenses increased.
We need to dig a hole.

35:05.000 --> 35:07.000
Arthur agreed to a plan
with a figure of 25.

35:08.600 --> 35:11.280
25 from 150 is 125.

35:11.360 --> 35:14.440
A third of that is £41,000.

35:15.960 --> 35:17.080
[scoffs]

35:18.440 --> 35:19.520
Sugar?

35:20.160 --> 35:21.160
Yes.

35:24.200 --> 35:25.960
[crockery clinking]

35:27.520 --> 35:28.840
Thank you.

35:30.640 --> 35:32.280
[Tommy clears throat]

35:36.600 --> 35:39.120
So, you've worked this all out, I see?

35:39.720 --> 35:42.320
Only in my head.
I haven't written it down.

35:44.120 --> 35:46.320
Linda, are you saying...

35:49.000 --> 35:50.760
if it were 41,000--

35:50.840 --> 35:54.320
I've already told you,
that'll be Arthur's decision.

35:55.680 --> 35:58.440
But I don't imagine
he'll accept less than 41.

36:01.600 --> 36:03.320
-May I smoke?
-No.

36:10.600 --> 36:12.320
So, I imagine you have some plans

36:13.880 --> 36:15.360
for your 41,000.

36:16.400 --> 36:18.720
Yes. California.

36:19.480 --> 36:21.720
For the child's health,
away from the smoke.

36:22.240 --> 36:24.800
We want to run a general store
on an Indian mission.

36:25.440 --> 36:28.560
The Americans invite Quakers
to do good work with the Indians.

36:29.800 --> 36:32.120
We've already sent our papers
and been accepted.

36:33.400 --> 36:34.840
[chuckles]

36:34.920 --> 36:36.960
Arthur Shelby as a missionary...

36:37.040 --> 36:40.360
-No. Arthur will run the store.
-Hmm.

36:41.080 --> 36:42.960
I will teach in the school next to it.

36:44.120 --> 36:47.920
Arthur will swim in the ocean.
I will be on the beach with the towel.

36:48.000 --> 36:51.440
The open air and the sun will get rid of
all the nonsense in his head from France.

36:55.360 --> 36:56.840
That's some plan.

36:57.760 --> 36:59.320
As you know yourself,

37:00.760 --> 37:04.240
the arrival of a new life
concentrates the mind on practical things.

37:04.720 --> 37:06.160
Amen to that.

37:09.600 --> 37:10.800
When is the child due?

37:11.080 --> 37:12.320
September.

37:12.880 --> 37:14.000
When is the robbery?

37:15.240 --> 37:16.360
June.

37:17.960 --> 37:19.840
Then the timing's perfect.

37:21.840 --> 37:23.520
We'll book a passage
through the Panama Canal

37:23.600 --> 37:26.480
the day after
the 41,000 is paid to Arthur.

37:26.560 --> 37:27.760
[coughing]

37:29.360 --> 37:31.720
Did we agree 41,000, Linda?

37:32.680 --> 37:34.320
I heard nothing to the contrary.

37:37.160 --> 37:40.120
-[Ruben] Word association. Right now.
-Oh, God. I hate this game.

37:40.200 --> 37:41.600
It's Freud. It's terribly fashionable.

37:41.680 --> 37:44.280
I'd rather you put on
that music that I hate.

37:44.360 --> 37:46.960
[sighs] Are we going mad
in here, do you think?

37:47.040 --> 37:48.080
Yes.

37:48.320 --> 37:50.960
[chuckles] We shouldn't have drunk
red wine with the cake.

37:51.440 --> 37:55.240
And I believe your vow never to sleep
with another man is a good one.

37:55.880 --> 37:57.160
Good for the painting.

37:58.200 --> 38:00.160
It's not a vow. It's just...

38:01.360 --> 38:04.800
I think when men want sex,
they become hilarious.

38:05.920 --> 38:10.560
Like a dog, when you pick up a lead,
and he knows he's going for a walk.

38:15.560 --> 38:17.880
Well, may I respectfully point out

38:18.280 --> 38:22.760
that so far you haven't even
picked up the bloody lead.

38:28.040 --> 38:29.080
There.

38:31.960 --> 38:33.120
That's the look.

38:33.800 --> 38:35.000
Imperious.

38:36.680 --> 38:39.160
No man is good enough.

38:59.360 --> 39:01.440
[children talking]

39:04.760 --> 39:06.680
-[roars]
-[all screaming]

39:10.440 --> 39:12.040
[indistinct chatter]

39:47.840 --> 39:49.520
[water dripping]

40:14.960 --> 40:16.400
[grunting]

40:45.880 --> 40:47.360
[both grunting]

40:49.560 --> 40:51.160
[screaming]

40:53.320 --> 40:54.480
[crack]

40:55.880 --> 40:56.880
[thud]

40:59.800 --> 41:01.280
[engine idling]

41:18.280 --> 41:19.960
[inhales sharply]

41:43.520 --> 41:48.560
[Jarvis] You idiot. You nearly killed him.
I told you we needed him fully conscious.

41:49.240 --> 41:52.960
We need to stop using soldiers
who've been in India, they hit too hard.

41:53.040 --> 41:54.520
[Hughes] Not fucking hard enough.

41:54.600 --> 41:56.400
Hey, Mr. Shelby. Hey.

41:56.480 --> 42:01.640
I heard about your plan to kill a holy man
from a voice in the confessional.

42:01.720 --> 42:02.880
[Jarvis] Can you hear us?

42:02.960 --> 42:04.160
[groans]

42:04.360 --> 42:05.400
Grace?

42:05.840 --> 42:07.040
Shelby.

42:08.680 --> 42:10.960
Why were you attempting
to kill Father Hughes?

42:13.120 --> 42:15.760
Maybe we should wait
until he is fully conscious.

42:15.840 --> 42:17.480
I have a dinner appointment.

42:18.160 --> 42:19.880
Hey, Shelby?

42:20.280 --> 42:22.080
Wake up. Eyes front.

42:22.160 --> 42:23.280
[breathing heavily]

42:23.360 --> 42:26.000
Mr. Shelby, you're trying to kill me,
were you?

42:27.920 --> 42:29.360
Passing information...

42:30.160 --> 42:32.000
[Jarvis] Fuck. He knows.

42:37.240 --> 42:38.400
Where am I?

42:39.160 --> 42:43.240
You are among the Odd Fellows.
Please count from ten to one.

42:43.720 --> 42:45.040
Ah, fuck you.

43:07.920 --> 43:12.280
Whatever else you might have forgotten
about last night,

43:13.040 --> 43:14.160
remember this.

43:15.600 --> 43:18.400
I am passing on information
to the Soviet Embassy

43:18.920 --> 43:20.640
on the instruction of Section D.

43:21.840 --> 43:24.040
It's part of a bigger picture.

43:24.480 --> 43:28.880
You explain to the Russians
that you were mistaken about me,

43:29.160 --> 43:32.000
and you apologize to me in front of them.

43:35.080 --> 43:37.920
A threat on your sister
was evidently not enough.

43:38.360 --> 43:41.880
You do as we say,
or we will take your son.

43:42.840 --> 43:46.440
Hear this. We will take your son.

43:47.040 --> 43:48.880
We can do it at any moment.

43:49.480 --> 43:51.960
We have people in your life.

43:56.080 --> 43:59.200
You will make your apology to me
tomorrow night,

44:00.600 --> 44:03.240
and you will repair the damage
you've done.

44:04.120 --> 44:06.600
[echoing] Or you will never
see your son again.

44:19.200 --> 44:20.400
[groaning]

44:32.480 --> 44:33.960
[door opens]

44:34.040 --> 44:35.680
[Mary] Sir, I don't understand...

44:35.760 --> 44:37.480
[Tommy panting]

44:37.560 --> 44:40.960
I don't understand why,
as a former soldier yourself,

44:41.040 --> 44:43.800
you have sacked all of the former
soldiers on the staff.

44:43.880 --> 44:45.880
It means there is only one man
left in the household.

44:45.960 --> 44:48.920
Mary, I want it so that
Charles is never left on his own.

44:49.000 --> 44:50.080
Understood?

44:51.200 --> 44:53.040
Sir, I should call a doctor.

44:53.120 --> 44:55.680
There will be some men coming.
Coming down from Birmingham.

44:56.040 --> 44:57.640
And you put them up here in the house.

44:57.720 --> 45:00.520
You put them in the front and back of
the house, you feed them, and you...

45:00.640 --> 45:01.920
Why are they needed, sir?

45:02.640 --> 45:05.560
I brought a cursed sapphire
into this house, Mary.

45:06.240 --> 45:07.920
And now, I'm paying for it.

45:10.680 --> 45:12.680
And I don't know what to expect.

45:13.680 --> 45:15.720
But neither do my enemies.

45:16.240 --> 45:18.920
Tell David to bring the car around.
I need to go to London.

45:19.280 --> 45:21.840
-Sir...
-And get me some tea, Mary.

45:24.360 --> 45:25.640
Yes, sir.

45:26.800 --> 45:27.800
[door opens]

45:49.280 --> 45:51.000
-[phone clicks]
-[Arthur on phone] Hello?

45:51.080 --> 45:52.680
-Yes, Arthur.
-Tommy?

45:54.240 --> 45:57.720
They want the robbery to be sabotaged.

45:58.240 --> 45:59.960
They don't give a fuck who gets hurt.

46:00.040 --> 46:01.080
Are you okay, Tommy?

46:01.160 --> 46:03.160
-It's a bigger picture now.
-What...

46:04.000 --> 46:05.160
Did John make a list?

46:05.240 --> 46:06.720
Speak clearer, Tom.

46:06.800 --> 46:08.040
I said did John make a list?

46:08.120 --> 46:10.120
John-Boy! John!

46:10.200 --> 46:11.280
Right.

46:11.600 --> 46:14.880
Gypsies and kin only. Yeah.

46:14.960 --> 46:16.120
Good.

46:16.880 --> 46:19.080
Tommy, can I ask you why?

46:19.160 --> 46:20.240
Tommy?

46:22.720 --> 46:24.240
[phone ringing]

46:24.320 --> 46:27.040
No, Karl. I told you.
Go on and play in there.

46:30.480 --> 46:31.520
Hello?

46:33.000 --> 46:36.880
[sighs] Ada, it's me. It's Tommy.

46:38.280 --> 46:39.680
Ada, I need you to...

46:40.440 --> 46:43.240
I need you to speak
to one of your comrades

46:43.320 --> 46:46.720
and get me a meeting
with someone from the Soviet Embassy.

46:48.000 --> 46:49.240
Tonight.

46:49.560 --> 46:51.560
Your place, 10:00 p.m.

46:56.560 --> 46:58.040
[retching]

47:00.960 --> 47:05.720
It seems that Mr. Shelby
was given bad information by an informant

47:06.200 --> 47:08.640
who was also in contact
with the underwriter,

47:09.840 --> 47:13.120
who, as we know,
is in the pocket of the Soviets.

47:14.880 --> 47:17.320
-Wine, Tatiana?
-A little.

47:20.040 --> 47:21.360
Bad girl.

47:24.960 --> 47:26.600
[sniffing]

47:42.760 --> 47:44.200
[door opens]

47:48.120 --> 47:49.280
[door closes]

47:52.360 --> 47:53.800
[sniffles]

47:53.880 --> 47:55.680
[Tommy] Sorry I'm late. I, uh...

47:58.800 --> 48:01.680
There was a body on the line.
[clears throat]

48:02.080 --> 48:03.360
Drink, Mr. Shelby?

48:04.280 --> 48:05.480
No, thank you.

48:05.560 --> 48:07.240
It was drink that caused
half this trouble.

48:08.280 --> 48:10.840
I have come here to apologize.

48:12.200 --> 48:14.720
I have already explained
that you now realize

48:14.800 --> 48:19.360
that your absurd allegation against me
was false.

48:20.240 --> 48:21.400
Indeed.

48:21.800 --> 48:24.720
[Hughes] And that your base nature
made you rash.

48:25.120 --> 48:26.320
[sniffles]

48:27.280 --> 48:30.760
And that now, once again,
our plan is back on track.

48:32.160 --> 48:35.120
When a child in my care commits a sin,

48:36.640 --> 48:39.520
first of all, he confesses,
as you just did.

48:40.000 --> 48:42.880
And then,
I instruct him to perform penance

48:43.560 --> 48:45.480
in a manner of my choosing.

48:45.960 --> 48:47.560
As a child, you went to church?

48:48.600 --> 48:49.680
Yes.

48:49.760 --> 48:51.720
[Hughes] Do you remember
the Act of Contrition?

48:53.560 --> 48:54.840
Good.

48:54.920 --> 48:56.760
Do you remember
the words of the Act of Contrition?

48:58.600 --> 48:59.800
[clears throat] Yes.

49:02.400 --> 49:05.520
As your penance,
I would like you to recite it now,

49:06.640 --> 49:08.640
in the presence of our associates.

49:10.560 --> 49:11.760
[door opens]

49:14.040 --> 49:15.360
Go away.

49:17.440 --> 49:18.760
[Tommy clears throat]

49:19.720 --> 49:20.720
[door closes]

49:21.360 --> 49:22.560
Uh...

49:27.080 --> 49:30.400
Oh, my God,
I am heartily sorry for having--

49:30.480 --> 49:32.680
[Hughes] Instead of "God," say my name.

49:33.440 --> 49:36.400
Since it was me you offended
with your false allegation.

49:40.280 --> 49:43.760
Father Hughes, I am heartily sorry
for having offended you,

49:47.360 --> 49:48.640
because of your just punishment,

49:48.720 --> 49:50.560
but most of all, because they offend you.

49:53.400 --> 49:57.160
Father Hughes, who art all good
and deserving of my love,

49:57.880 --> 49:59.000
[sighs]

50:00.000 --> 50:01.600
I firmly resolve to...

50:04.040 --> 50:06.280
With the help of your grace,
to sin no more

50:06.360 --> 50:09.360
and to avoid all near occasions of sin.

50:10.640 --> 50:11.720
Mmm.

50:14.440 --> 50:17.200
Very good. Thank you.

50:18.240 --> 50:19.400
Amen.

50:22.720 --> 50:23.800
[sighs]

50:26.160 --> 50:30.240
And now that we are
a united band once more,

50:30.320 --> 50:32.240
perhaps we could order some food.

50:33.480 --> 50:36.320
I'm sorry. I am not feeling well.
I have to go. Good night.

50:37.880 --> 50:39.200
Mr. Shelby...

50:45.920 --> 50:47.200
[sniffling]

50:48.160 --> 50:49.160
My God, Tommy.

50:49.240 --> 50:50.280
-Are they here?
-Yeah.

50:50.720 --> 50:52.760
-Do you have cocaine?
-No.

50:52.840 --> 50:54.520
-[sighs]
-Tommy.

50:57.200 --> 51:00.280
Uh, Tommy, this is the Special Adviser
to the Soviet Consul.

51:08.440 --> 51:12.640
Members of the British establishment
and exiled White Russians

51:12.720 --> 51:16.560
are planning to rob armored cars
from a factory in Birmingham.

51:16.680 --> 51:19.200
We know about the robbery.
We have an informant.

51:19.280 --> 51:22.280
No, your informant is working for them.
They want you to know about the robbery.

51:24.920 --> 51:26.000
[speaking Russian]

51:26.080 --> 51:27.560
Your informant is working for them.

51:27.760 --> 51:30.800
They want you to know about the robbery.

51:31.040 --> 51:33.640
[in English] Your informant
is working to their instruction.

51:34.920 --> 51:36.240
[speaking Russian]

51:36.320 --> 51:38.760
Your informant is working
to their instructions.

51:40.080 --> 51:42.000
[in English]
Why would they want us to know?

51:42.080 --> 51:43.400
They want you to...

51:44.240 --> 51:46.240
They want you to stop the robbery.

51:46.320 --> 51:49.640
They want you to commit a violent act
on British soil.

51:49.720 --> 51:50.880
Tommy, do you want water?

51:51.320 --> 51:52.760
A violent act on British...

51:53.920 --> 51:55.120
[Dimitri speaking Russian]

51:55.200 --> 51:56.360
...violent acts on British soil.

51:57.240 --> 51:58.400
[sighs]

51:59.800 --> 52:00.920
[in English] To force
the British government

52:01.000 --> 52:03.280
to break off diplomatic relations.

52:03.600 --> 52:05.120
[Dimitri speaking Russian]

52:05.200 --> 52:07.360
To force the government
to break diplomatic relations.

52:07.440 --> 52:09.120
[sniffles] That's the game.

52:10.640 --> 52:12.520
The robbery in Birmingham
is just the bait.

52:12.960 --> 52:14.360
[Dimitri speaking Russian]

52:14.440 --> 52:16.880
Birmingham robbery is purely bait.

52:17.000 --> 52:18.840
[in English] Why are you telling us this?

52:19.680 --> 52:22.320
Because my family are the ones
who will be sacrificed

52:23.360 --> 52:25.200
if you decide to blow up the train.

52:25.600 --> 52:26.840
[Dimitri speaking Russian]

52:26.920 --> 52:28.480
Because my family would be killed

52:28.560 --> 52:31.400
if you decide to blow up the train.

52:31.840 --> 52:34.280
[in English] The Consul wants to know
who you are.

52:35.520 --> 52:36.800
He's Tommy Shelby.

52:37.160 --> 52:39.040
You can take his word.

52:39.120 --> 52:40.680
-[Tommy] Ada.
-Tommy...

52:40.760 --> 52:41.880
Ada.

52:42.280 --> 52:43.360
Okay.

52:43.680 --> 52:45.240
[Ada grunting]

52:49.200 --> 52:50.640
Stop, stop.

52:50.720 --> 52:52.520
Ada, stop.

52:52.880 --> 52:54.960
[grunts] Okay.

52:57.880 --> 52:59.440
Drive me to a hospital, Ada.

53:00.720 --> 53:04.320
If I'm not conscious when I get there,
tell them I have a fractured skull,

53:04.400 --> 53:06.040
concussion and internal bleeding.

53:06.520 --> 53:07.960
I think I may have hemorrhaged.

53:08.040 --> 53:09.400
-Tommy.
-Ada, go on.

53:09.480 --> 53:10.800
-Be quick because I can't see.
-Okay.

53:10.880 --> 53:12.280
I can't fucking see.

53:13.360 --> 53:15.040
[sobs] Okay. Okay.

53:23.400 --> 53:25.160
Except for you, Dad.

53:30.040 --> 53:31.520
I can see you.

54:05.920 --> 54:08.280
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

54:08.360 --> 54:10.160
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

54:10.240 --> 54:12.320
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

54:12.400 --> 54:14.680
♪ A red right hand ♪
